(* People have devised many clever ways to represent dates and times. *)

// date "input" -- what can SenseTalk recognize as a date?

put "April 1, 1926" is a date
put "4/1/26" is a date
put "4 APR 1926" is a date
put "1926-04-01" is a date
put -

// date "output" -- what date formats can SenseTalk produce?

put today

put the date
put short date
put the abbreviated date
put the long date
put -
put the common date
put the international date
put the internet date
put the simple date
put -
put the long common date
put the long international date
put the long internet date
put the long simple date
put -
